course: dictionary
lesson: 10838
title: Finding the meaning of verdict
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A verdict is a decision made at the end of something. In a court, the verdict is the decision of the jury or judge, such as guilty or not guilty. «The verdict is the jury's decision, guilty or not guilty.»
explain: Verdict can also mean an everyday opinion, the judgement you make after trying something. «What's your verdict on the pizza?» asks what you think of it after you have tasted it.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. If the sentence mentions a jury, a judge, witnesses or a trial, it is a court decision. If it is about a film, food or a game, it is an opinion. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Verdict is a noun, so you can write a verdict or verdicts.
fact: «Verdict» means the decision of a jury or judge in a court case, such as guilty or not guilty.
fact: «Verdict» can also mean an opinion or judgement after trying something, as in «What's your verdict on the pizza?»
fact: Useful phrases: «reach a verdict», «a guilty verdict», «the verdict is in».
fact: The verdict is not the same as the sentence: the verdict is the decision, and the sentence is the punishment the judge gives after a guilty verdict.
exercise: «Witnesses tell what they saw, and then the jury gives its verdict: guilty or not guilty.» In this sentence, what is a verdict? | A house where people live | *A decision made by the jury | A loud shout in the court | A witness who saw the crime
exercise: Sam sits on the bench all match and asks «Did I even play?» Coaches pick for many reasons, so sitting out once is not a verdict on him. What does verdict mean here? | A court decision about a crime | A list of the players' names | *An opinion or judgement about how good he is | A kind of football shirt
exercise: «What's your verdict on the pizza?» What is the person asking? | How much the pizza cost | Where the pizza was made | *What you think of it, after trying it | Whether you are guilty of eating it
test: The judge tells the jury they must reach a verdict before the trial ends. What does reach a verdict mean? | Stop listening to the witnesses | Ask for a drink of water | Walk out of the room | *Come to a final decision
test: «The King turns pale and says, "Consider your verdict."» What does the King want the jury to do? | Sing a song to the court | Go home for lunch | *Decide their final judgement | Read the note-book out loud
exam: Which sentence uses verdict as an opinion rather than a court decision? | *«What's your verdict on the new film?» | «The verdict was read out in court.» | «The judge reached a verdict after one hour.» | «The jury gave a guilty verdict.»
